%I A399241 #13 Sep 03 2026 17:53:44
%S A399241 1,1,0,0,0,0,101,5436428,1166118906529401
%N A399241 Number of isomorphism classes of asymmetric maximal intersecting families of subsets of an n-element set.
%C A399241 Equivalently, a(n) is the number of equivalence classes, under permutations of variables, of n-variable monotone self-dual Boolean functions with trivial automorphism group.
%C A399241 The values were obtained by Mobius inversion on the subgroup lattice of S_n, using fixed-point counts F_n(H) for maximal intersecting families invariant under H <= S_n.
%D A399241 V. Jovovic and G. Kilibarda, On the number of Boolean functions in the Post classes F_8^mu, Diskretnaya Matematika 11 (1999), no. 4, 127-138; English translation in Discrete Mathematics and Applications 9 (1999), no. 6.
%D A399241 B. Pawelski and A. Szepietowski, Self-dual monotone Boolean functions, Journal of Integer Sequences 28 (2025).
%H A399241 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A399241/a399241.pdf">Asymmetric Maximal Intersecting Families of Subsets: Möbius Inversion and Computation</a>.
%H A399241 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A399241/a399241.g.txt">GAP program for a(7)</a>
%F A399241 a(n) = Sum_{[H] <= S_n} mu(1,H)*F_n(H)/|N_{S_n}(H)|, where the sum is over conjugacy classes of subgroups H of S_n, mu is the subgroup-lattice Mobius function, and F_n(H) is the number of maximal intersecting families fixed by H.
%F A399241 n!*a(n) = Sum_{H <= S_n} mu(1,H)*F_n(H).
%e A399241 a(3)=0 since every maximal intersecting family on a 3-element set has a nontrivial automorphism.
%e A399241 a(7)=101, so there are 101 isomorphism classes of maximal intersecting families on a 7-element set with trivial automorphism group.
%Y A399241 Cf. A001206, A008840, A107765, A059090, A305856, A305857.
%K A399241 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A399241 1,7
